@@ -24,6 +24,7 @@ package, not for somebody reading this repository's commit log.
 
 ### Fixed
 
+- `onError` now fires for every rejection, not only when the thrown value is already an `Error`. A string, plain object, `undefined`, or any other non-`Error` rejection is wrapped in a new `Error` whose `cause` carries the original value, so a hook typed against `Error` keeps compiling and a hook that wants the raw value can still reach it via `error.cause`. The value the caller receives is unchanged — it is still the original rejection, not the wrapper. Previously, a non-`Error` rejection bypassed `onError` entirely while still propagating to the caller. **Migration note**: hooks that check `error instanceof SomeSubclass` still work; hooks that look for specific `.message` text on a non-`Error` rejection (which previously never fired) should now look in `error.cause` instead.
 - `onError` and `afterSession` hooks now fire when `beforeSession` throws, matching the guarantee the hook names imply. Previously, a throw from `beforeSession` escaped the `try`/`finally` block entirely, so neither hook ran. **Migration note**: if your `afterSession` hook assumed it would only be called after a full session turn, it will now also be called when `beforeSession` itself fails — the hook can inspect the session to detect this case (no entries beyond the initial user message will have been processed).
 
